Upstream commit the port matches:
  7a17182bbb21e3e0aeb0c4f777794afc754bde69   2026-11-23T21:21:35+01:00

The port's first commit matched 0ac6495 (2026-11-09). The port forward to 7a17182 (2026-11-23) is a work in
progress: the per-file lines below say, file by file, what of the newer upstream is in the port, what is still NOT
STARTED, and what of it this engine cannot take (ENGINE). A line that says nothing of the newer upstream describes
the port at 0ac6495 (the newer changes are not ported yet); a line naming a newer feature says it is ported.
The port forward is measured in stages (see the paragraph after the map).

How to port forward: diff the upstream files below against that commit (git diff 0ac6495..HEAD -- dll/ai/<file>)
and carry the changed decisions into the Lua module named. The port keeps the decisions (budgets, targets, timings,
the force's rules), not the engine patches: what upstream patches into the original exe (danger routes, honest
vision, the group move, the unload retries) is a C++ helper of this engine (docs/AI_LUA_UNITS.md §4, §11).

From 0ac6495 to 7a17182 upstream added ~20k lines and 24 files. Most of the newer AI plays only with the game's own
computer player off ([ai_base] game_ai = 0, upstream's default since 2026-11-14): its own economy (work.c, build.c,
research.c, savings.c, claims.c), the force by territory (territories.c, stations.c, produce.c, army_view.c,
claims.c), the ferry service and crossings (ferry.c, crossing.c, convoy.c, explore.c), the air guard (airguard.c,
storms.c), the squadrons (squadrons.c), the holy units (holy.c), the strategy plans (plans.c, returns.c), and the
pieces the territories carry (watch.c, creep.c, news.c, scen_targets.c). The probe before porting one of those is
the engine: this engine exposes no territory split (game/territory.c is retail), no stance-claimed unit ownership
(claims.c), no unit improvements through a Lua call to the game's improve verb where the data lacks it, no
territory graph for the ferry, and no personality leanings. Where a decision needs one of those, the port either
stands in with its own cheap model (a cell grid built from ai.tile, as fronts.lua does) or says ENGINE.

